<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hashimids of Derbent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">869–<a href="/years/1075">1075</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Hashimid dynasty of Derbent</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hashimids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derbent">Derbent</a> were an Arab dynasty that ruled the city of Derbent on the Caspian coast as hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> from 869 to 1075. Founded by the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hashim-ibn-suraqa">Hashim ibn Suraqa</a> as Abbasid authority weakened, the family gradually became a local power, fighting and allying with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirvanshah">Shirvanshahs</a> and neighbouring Caucasian peoples. Their history survives in a local chronicle preserved by the Ottoman historian Münejjimbashi.</p></div>
